<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sultan Shah ibn Ridwan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Shah ibn Ridwan was the last Seljuk ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, a son of Ridwan. He succeeded his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alp-arslan-al-akhras">Alp Arslan al-Akhras</a> in 1114 but was a puppet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> Lu'lu' and other officers. Threatened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>, the notables of Aleppo turned to outside protectors, and the Artuqid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilghazi">Ilghazi</a> took over the city in 1118.</p></div>
